#!/usr/bin/env bash

##	- Purpose: git pre-push hook. Runs the merge gate (cicd.bash --merge-gate)
##	  when a push updates main, so nothing reaches it unchecked. A push to dev
##	  or any other branch, and a delete, goes straight through.
##	- A push to main that changes only the paths MERGE_GATE_SKIP in
##	  cicd/config.bash names, such as docs no build or test reads, skips it too.
##	- cicd.bash puts a stub in .git/hooks/pre-push that calls this, once per clone.
##	- The gate checks the working tree, so commit or stash stray edits first.
##	- CICD_GATE_PASSED=1 skips it; the pipeline sets that when it publishes, since
##	  it just ran the full tests.

